  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 38. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. 下水道 — 使った水や雨水を集めて流す仕組み。\n2. ゲスト — 招かれた客や出演者。\n3. 月光 — 月から届く光。\n4. 月謝 — 教えてもらうために毎月払うお金。\n5. 月末 — 月の終わりごろ。\n6. ゲレンデ — スキーなどをするために整えた斜面。\n7. 原画 — 印刷や映像などのもとになる絵。\n8. 弦楽器 — 弦を振動させて音を出す楽器。\n9. 原型 — 物を作るときのもとになる形。\n10. 原稿 — 発表したり印刷したりするために書いた文章など。\n11. 言語 — 人が考えや気持ちを伝え合うための言葉の仕組み。\n12. 元号 — 令和などの年を表すために定められた名前。\n13. 原産地 — その品物などがもともと生まれたり作られたりする土地。\n14. 原材料 — 製品や料理などを作るもとになる材料。\n15. 原色 — ほかの色を混ぜて作るときのもとになる色。\n16. 現実 — 実際にあることや起きていること。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\nDo not add numerical claims, prices, quantities, currency denominations, calorie values or stroke-order numbers unless explicitly required by the target word. Mathematical concepts should have neutral concrete examples without unverified numeric diagrams.\n",
